Both gates pass cleanly. Summary:

Converted the four free functions in `logger.rs` to idiomatic Rust shapes per the project's "free functions on a primary `&T`/`&mut T` argument become methods" rule. `set_textlog` and `textlog_close` are now inherent methods on `Quic`; `log_fin_or_event_name` becomes `CallbackEvent::name(self) -> &'static str` (the C name's `log_fin_or_event_` prefix was redundant once the function lives on the enum). `textlog_tls_ticket` stays a free function because its primary argument is the writer, not a domain type — but the `textlog_` prefix was dropped (`write_tls_ticket`) since the `crate::logger` module path already conveys "this is the textlog backend's helper" and the function makes no internal reference to a textlog state. Also tidied the orphan trailing comment fragment after `set_textlog`'s former doc block, refreshed the module-level doc to point at the new method paths, and updated the cross-reference in `binlog.rs`. The `C:` traceability lines were updated to use the unaltered C symbol names (`picoquic_set_textlog`, etc.) rather than the post-translation Rust names.


